From 1113423c150505d24cb1a292adea00b1bab6ead1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Captain Polliwog build <build@captainpolliwog.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:08:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] JavaScript: class fields, private members, logical
 assignment, import.meta

- Public class fields, instance and static (ES2022). Each class gets a
  generated initializer function whose source is the class body; when it
  is compiled the parser reads only the recorded field positions.
  Constructors run it on entry (base classes) or after super() returns.
- Private members (#name): fields, methods, accessors, static ones, and
  '#name in obj'. Each private name is a constant in the class scope
  holding a new symbol per class evaluation, and obj.#name compiles to
  obj[that symbol]. No brand check: a missing private name reads as
  undefined rather than throwing.
- Logical assignment &&=, ||= and ??= (ES2021).
- import.meta, with the module's url (ES2020).
- await directly after a unary operator (void await x, !await x), which
  the 604 parser read as an identifier.
